This package statically links the Rust crates whose sources are shipped in
src/rust/vendor.tar.xz. Their authorship and licences are listed below; the
versions are those recorded in src/rust/Cargo.lock.

Licences appearing among these dependencies:
  - (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0
  - Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0
  - MIT
  - MIT OR Apache-2.0

Note that unicode-ident additionally carries the Unicode-3.0 licence for its
embedded Unicode character tables (its SPDX expression is reproduced verbatim
below). Full licence texts are included in each crate's directory inside
src/rust/vendor.tar.xz.

When Cargo is unavailable on the build machine a pre-compiled binary may be
used instead; it is compiled from these same sources, so the authorship and
licences are unchanged.

The test suite additionally contains a verbatim port of jsonlite's own toJSON
tests (tests/testthat/test-jsonlite-*.R), used to verify that as_json() is a
drop-in replacement for jsonlite::toJSON(). Those files are test code only;
no jsonlite code is linked into or distributed with the package binary.

Name:    jsonlite (test suite only)
Files:   tests/testthat/test-jsonlite-*.R
Authors: Jeroen Ooms and jsonlite contributors
License: MIT
Source:  jsonlite 2.0.0, tests/testthat/test-toJSON-*.R and
         test-libjson-{escaping,utf8}.R

